In `pkg/plugins/log/logger.go`, `grafanaInfraLogWrapper.FromContext` attempts `d.l.FromContext(ctx).(*log.ConcreteLogger)` and if that fails it falls back to `return d.New()`.

```go
concreteInfraLogger, ok := d.l.FromContext(ctx).(*log.ConcreteLogger)
if !ok {
    return d.New()
}
```

This fallback ignores the provided `ctx` entirely, so any contextual attributes carried in `ctx` are dropped (and there’s no log/error indicating the type mismatch). That matches the finding’s mechanism about silently losing contextual logging and masking wiring regressions.

